{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function resolveModifier(modifier, platform?): CanonicalModifier;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/platform.ts#L58","children":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.ts:58"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resolves the platform-adaptive 'Mod' modifier to the appropriate canonical modifier."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The 'Mod' token represents the \"primary modifier\" on each platform:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"macOS: 'Meta' (Command key ⌘)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Windows/Linux: 'Control' (Ctrl key)"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This enables cross-platform hotkey definitions like 'Mod+S' that automatically\nmap to Command+S on Mac and Ctrl+S on Windows/Linux."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"modifier","children":[{"type":"text","value":"modifier"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"Mod\""},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/CanonicalModifier.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CanonicalModifier"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The modifier to resolve. If 'Mod', resolves based on platform."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"platform","children":[{"type":"text","value":"platform?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"mac\""},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"windows\""},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"linux\""}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The target platform. Defaults to auto-detection."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/CanonicalModifier.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CanonicalModifier"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The canonical modifier name ('Control', 'Shift', 'Alt', or 'Meta')"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"resolveModifier('Mod', 'mac') // 'Meta'\nresolveModifier('Mod', 'windows') // 'Control'\nresolveModifier('Control', 'mac') // 'Control' (unchanged)","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"modifier","text":"modifier","level":3},{"id":"platform","text":"platform?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction resolveModifier(modifier, platform?): CanonicalModifier;\n```\n\nDefined in: [platform.ts:58](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/platform.ts#L58)\n\nResolves the platform-adaptive 'Mod' modifier to the appropriate canonical modifier.\n\nThe 'Mod' token represents the \"primary modifier\" on each platform:\n- macOS: 'Meta' (Command key ⌘)\n- Windows/Linux: 'Control' (Ctrl key)\n\nThis enables cross-platform hotkey definitions like 'Mod+S' that automatically\nmap to Command+S on Mac and Ctrl+S on Windows/Linux.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### modifier\n\n`\"Mod\"` \\| [`CanonicalModifier`](../type-aliases/CanonicalModifier.md)\n\nThe modifier to resolve. If 'Mod', resolves based on platform.\n\n### platform?\n\n`\"mac\"` \\| `\"windows\"` \\| `\"linux\"`\n\nThe target platform. Defaults to auto-detection.\n\n## Returns\n\n[`CanonicalModifier`](../type-aliases/CanonicalModifier.md)\n\nThe canonical modifier name ('Control', 'Shift', 'Alt', or 'Meta')\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nresolveModifier('Mod', 'mac') // 'Meta'\nresolveModifier('Mod', 'windows') // 'Control'\nresolveModifier('Control', 'mac') // 'Control' (unchanged)\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: resolveModifier\ntitle: resolveModifier\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction resolveModifier(modifier, platform?): CanonicalModifier;\n```\n\nDefined in: [platform.ts:58](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/platform.ts#L58)\n\nResolves the platform-adaptive 'Mod' modifier to the appropriate canonical modifier.\n\nThe 'Mod' token represents the \"primary modifier\" on each platform:\n- macOS: 'Meta' (Command key ⌘)\n- Windows/Linux: 'Control' (Ctrl key)\n\nThis enables cross-platform hotkey definitions like 'Mod+S' that automatically\nmap to Command+S on Mac and Ctrl+S on Windows/Linux.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### modifier\n\n`\"Mod\"` \\| [`CanonicalModifier`](../type-aliases/CanonicalModifier.md)\n\nThe modifier to resolve. If 'Mod', resolves based on platform.\n\n### platform?\n\n`\"mac\"` \\| `\"windows\"` \\| `\"linux\"`\n\nThe target platform. Defaults to auto-detection.\n\n## Returns\n\n[`CanonicalModifier`](../type-aliases/CanonicalModifier.md)\n\nThe canonical modifier name ('Control', 'Shift', 'Alt', or 'Meta')\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nresolveModifier('Mod', 'mac') // 'Meta'\nresolveModifier('Mod', 'windows') // 'Control'\nresolveModifier('Control', 'mac') // 'Control' (unchanged)\n```\n"}
